.\" Written by hand from lib/common.sh (require_config, build_exclude_params)
.\" and libexec/dedupctl/*.sh; keep it in step with them.
.TH DEDUPCTL.BORGBACKUP 5 2026-11-08 "dedupctl" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
dedupctl.borgbackup, .borgbackup \- backup source configuration for dedupctl
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I <directory>/.borgbackup
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dedupctl init
writes
.I .borgbackup
into the directory it is to back up.
Every other command of
.BR dedupctl (1)
finds the nearest one in the current directory or its parents, changes
into the directory that holds it, and reads it with the shell's
.B source
builtin: the file is a bash script, run with the user's rights, and may
set any variable.
.PP
These variables are read:
.TP
.B BORG_REPO
The Borg repository.
Required by every command but
.BR init .
.B init
sets it to
.IR $BORG_BACKUP_ROOT/<name> .
.TP
.B SOURCE_DIR
What
.B backup
archives, relative to the directory of the file.
Required by
.BR backup ;
.B init
sets it to
.BR ./ .
.TP
.B EXCLUDES
A bash array of patterns
.B backup
passes to
.B borg create
as
.BI \-\-exclude " pattern"
each.
When it is not set the patterns are
.BR .cache ,
.B tmp
and
.BR __pycache__ .
.PP
A file that is missing, or that leaves a required variable empty, ends
the command with status 3.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
# Borg backup configuration for /home/user/papers
SOURCE_DIR="./"
BORG_REPO="/home/user/.borg_backups/!home!user!papers"
EXCLUDES=(".cache" "node_modules" "*.log")
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dedupctl (1),
.BR borg (1)
